asically an iron axe mounted on a long handle curved at one end. At Angkor Wat, the phka\'k is held in the hands of high-ranking warriors mounted on elephants or horses; it is still in use in the twentieth century for hunting or work in the forest. Crossbows were known, but are extremely rare in the reliefs.\''}], {'usage.total_tokens': 908, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 806})
