ally fought for Byzantium, where they were known as mourtatoi. Müsellems and yayas were at first paid wages, but by the time of Murat I (1359) they were normally given lands or fiefs in return for military service, the yayas also having special responsibility for the protection of roads and bridges." <br>Janissaries were paid a monthly salary.<br>The Janissary organization is believed to have started during the reign of Murat I.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 939, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 827})
